{"tool_name":"igsimulator","contents":["oeb","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"igsimulator","home":"http://yana-safonova.github.io/ig_simulator/","summary":"Tool for simulation of antibody repertoire and Ig-seq library. It is designed for testing and benchmarking tools for reconstruction of Ig repertoires.","addition_date":"2017-08-03T18:47:01Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-10T12:58:55Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:igsimulator","credit":[{"email":"safonova.yana@gmail.com","name":"Yana Safonova","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"https://github.com/yana-safonova"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://yana-safonova.github.io/ig_simulator/"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://yana-safonova.github.io/ig_simulator/ig_simulator_manual.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Modelling and simulation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2426"},{"term":"Protein sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2479"}]}],"name":"IgSimulator","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"mbs_import","publication":[{"metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 The Author 2015.Motivation: The recent introduction of next-generation sequencing technologies to antibody studies have resulted in a growing number of immunoinformatics tools for antibody repertoire analysis. However, benchmarking these newly emerging tools remains problematic since the gold standard datasets that are needed to validate these tools are typically not available. Results: Since simulating antibody repertoires is often the only feasible way to benchmark new immunoinformatics tools, we developed the IgSimulator tool that addresses various complications in generating realistic antibody repertoires. IgSimulator's code has modular structure and can be easily adapted to new requirements to simulation.","authors":[{"name":"Lapidus A."},{"name":"Lill J."},{"name":"Safonova Y."}],"citationCount